meta {
  name: 1. Sign In (Google)
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/sign-in/social
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "provider": "google",
    "callbackURL": "http://localhost:3000"
  }
}

docs {
  Bruno can't do the OAuth redirect/consent screen itself, so this step stays
  manual:

  1. Send this request. The response is `{ "url": "<google-oauth-url>" }`.
  2. Paste that `url` into a real browser tab and complete Google's consent
     screen. You need to already be signed into the Google account you want
     to use, in that browser.
  3. Google redirects back to the API's own callback
     (`/api/auth/callback/google`), which is where the Session cookie is
     actually set — on `localhost:4000`, since `AUTH_COOKIE_DOMAIN` isn't set
     locally. It then redirects to `callbackURL` above, which will likely
     404 since no page handles it yet — that's expected.
  4. In DevTools on that browser tab: Application → Cookies →
     `http://localhost:4000` → copy the value of `better-auth.session_token`.
  5. Open this collection's "Local" environment in Bruno and paste that value
     into the `sessionCookie` secret variable (the padlock icon next to a
     variable marks it secret — its value is kept out of this committed
     `.bru` file, stored only in your local Bruno settings).

  Once `sessionCookie` is set, "2. Get Session" and "3. Create API Key" both
  reuse it automatically via the `Cookie` header.
}
